@tradition sunrise-stretch
// Sunrise stretch (0.60.7, the user's pick): a gentle group stretch along the promenade windows before breakfast,
// Mondays, Wednesdays and Fridays. Anyone can join. wake: 15 (most traditions need an hour after waking).
// The deck architect may tag stretch spots by the windows (event: 'sunrise-stretch'); else the promenade benches.
k: 448
title: Sunrise stretch
when: weekly monday,wednesday,friday
at: 06:30-07:00
min: 15
wake: 15
venue: plaza
where: 3 room Promenade: bench
where: 3 room Lift plaza: bench
hold: none
who: early-riser 55%, runner 40%, gym-regular 35%, everyone 8%
from: The promenade

== mail
- Sunrise stretch tomorrow, {time}, along the promenade windows. Gentle, slow, before breakfast. Come in whatever you slept in.   #funny

== ask
- Sunrise stretch this morning. Gentle, I promise.
- Stretch by the windows before breakfast? Wakes you up better than tea.   #warm

== here
- Reach up. Hold it. And breathe.
- My back says thank you. My knees have notes.   #funny
- Look at the light on the hull.   #warm

== thanks
- You stretch with the early risers along the promenade windows. By breakfast you feel awake all the way through.   #warm

== chatter
- Sunrise stretch is the only reason I'm awake before seven.   #funny
- The promenade at half six is the quietest place aboard.   #warm
